178
00:18:02.870 --> 00:18:07.699
Carly Huitema (University of Guelph): It is also agnostic about the underlying network transport.

179
00:18:07.870 --> 00:18:16.770
Carly Huitema (University of Guelph): These innovations mean trust can span different trust domains and networks, helping make the trust spanning protocol universally useful as the market landscape evolves.

180
00:18:20.720 --> 00:18:24.439
Carly Huitema (University of Guelph): But there's another important part of trust, privacy.

181
00:18:24.740 --> 00:18:41.599
Carly Huitema (University of Guelph): TSP messages are sure to be a form to be from a true authenticated party to a true intended party untampered. But even if the content of the message is protected, information about the communication itself can reveal a lot. Knowing who is talking to whom and when can create a valuable trail of metadata.

182
00:18:41.600 --> 00:18:54.999
Carly Huitema (University of Guelph): TSP includes mechanisms designed to make that kind of correlation more difficult. Using techniques such as nested messages and intermediary routing, the way a message travels can be protected so an observer has less ability to correlate the sender and recipient.

