00:20:52.450 --> 00:21:05.119
Carly Huitema (University of Guelph): There are many different ways to establish digital identity and trust. Digital identifiers, digital credentials, certificates, and other systems can all provide valuable capabilities, but they don't necessarily speak the same language.

198
00:21:05.310 --> 00:21:10.560
Carly Huitema (University of Guelph): The Trust Spanning Protocol, or TSP, is designed to provide a common layer that connects them.

199
00:21:11.220 --> 00:21:23.210
Carly Huitema (University of Guelph): Instead of requiring everyone to use the same identity system, TSP allows different trust ecosystems to communicate with one another. Think of it as a universal bridge for digital trust.

